# FindDoctorAndAppointmentWidget Error Analysis

## Error Description
The widget implementation deviated from documentation by:
- Using a single `location` TextInput instead of hierarchical fields
- Missing Region -> Province -> City -> CAP structure
- Ignoring UI/UX patterns from documentation

## Root Causes
1. Incomplete documentation review
2. Over-simplification of functionality
3. Ignored UI/UX patterns

## Prevention Steps
1. Read all documentation files thoroughly
2. Implement hierarchical structure
3. Follow UI/UX patterns
4. Test against requirements

## Correct Implementation
```php
protected function getSearchStep(): array
{
    return [
        Wizard\Step::make('search')
            ->schema([
                Fieldset::make('dentist_search')
                    ->schema([
                        Select::make('region')
                            ->options(fn () => Region::all()->pluck('name', 'id'))
                            ->searchable()
                            ->required()
                            ->live()
                            ->afterStateUpdated(fn (Set $set) => $set('province', null)),
                        
                        Select::make('province')
                            ->options(fn (Get $get) => Province::where('region_id', $get('region'))->pluck('name', 'id'))
                            ->searchable()
                            ->required()
                            ->live()
                            ->afterStateUpdated(fn (Set $set) => $set('city', null))
                            ->visible(fn (Get $get) => filled($get('region'))),
                        
                        Select::make('city')
                            ->options(fn (Get $get) => City::where('province_id', $get('province'))->pluck('name', 'id'))
                            ->searchable()
                            ->required()
                            ->live()
                            ->afterStateUpdated(fn (Set $set) => $set('cap', null))
                            ->visible(fn (Get $get) => filled($get('province'))),
                        
                        Select::make('cap')
                            ->options(fn (Get $get) => Cap::where('city_id', $get('city'))->pluck('code', 'id'))
                            ->searchable()
                            ->required()
                            ->visible(fn (Get $get) => filled($get('city'))),
                    ]),
            ])
    ];
}
```

## Key Lessons
1. Documentation is the source of truth
2. Don't oversimplify functionality
3. Follow UI/UX patterns
4. Test against requirements
5. Maintain consistency with design
